sentences.text:
1. The present appeal has been filed by the appellant/convict under Section 374/386 Cr.P.C. against the judgment of conviction dated 11.09.2019 and order on sentence dated 23.09.2019 passed by Ld.
MM, North, Rohini Courts thereby convicting the appellant/convict as follows:
(i) For the offence under Section 304A IPC to undergo SI for one year and to pay fine of Rs.10,000/- and in default of payment of fine, SI for three months;
(ii) For the offence under Section 338 IPC to undergo SI for six months and to pay fine of Rs.1,000/- and in default of payment of fine, SI for two months;
(iii) For the offence under Section 337 IPC to undergo SI for three months and to pay fine of Rs.500/- and in default of payment of fine, SI for one month;
(iv) For the offence under Section 279 IPC to undergo SI for three months and to pay fine of Rs.500/- and in default of payment of fine, SI for one month;
2. Brief facts of the case are that on 07.11.2012 at about 8.45 p.m. at 800 Foota Road near CNG Petrol Pump, Narela, Delhi, accused Surender was found driving a tractor- trolley bearing Surender vs The State on 21 April, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/11458284/
1 registration no. HE-10N-7835 in a rash and negligent manner so as to endanger human life and personal safety of others and while driving so, he hit the abovesaid tractor against one Maruti Van bearing registration no. DL-3CR-4231 due to which the passengers of such car namely one Harpal sustained simple injuries; Praveen sustained grievous injuries and Manoj also sustained injuries but later on succumbed to the same.

18. The appellant has been convicted as follows:
(i) For the offence under Section 304A IPC to undergo SI for one year and to pay fine of Rs.10,000/- and in default of payment of fine, SI for three months;
(ii) For the offence under Section 338 IPC to undergo SI for six months and to pay fine of Rs.1,000/- and in default of payment of fine, SI for two months;
(iii) For the offence under Section 337 IPC to undergo SI for three months and to pay fine of Rs.500/- and in default of payment of fine, SI for one month;
(iv) For the offence under Section 279 IPC to undergo SI for three months and to pay fine of Rs.500/- and in default of payment of fine, SI for one month;
19.

, the sentence is altered to the extent that the appellant Surender be sentenced for a fine of Rs.80,000/-, which may be released to the injured persons as follows:
(a) Harpal Rs.10,000/- ;
(b) Parveen Rs. 10,000/- ;
(c) Rs.60,000/- in total proportionately to the LRs of deceased  Manoj;
as compensation by the Ld. Trial Court as per rules in terms of Section 357 (1) Cr.P.C upon giving the notice to the injured persons and LRs of deceased Manoj and in default of payment of fine simple imprisonment for 15 days.

